 in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y) = 20-x^2-y^2.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{1,2,3\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{0,1,2\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the lower Riemann sum $L(f,P).$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152148 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-73bd1c38-9ed6-5451-94fd-2aa984462a1e"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186151936 :question/problem "Let $R = [0,2] \\times [1,3]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y) = x+2y.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{0,1,2\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{1,2,3\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the lower Riemann sum $L(f,P).$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-f89ca459-c179-53fe-83c0-45ad6670695a" :question/id #uuid "f89ca459-c179-53fe-83c0-45ad6670695a" :question/math-academy-id "q-122874" :question/problem "![](images/03/03935d4a02a1a42a106e148fa120132a246818684f88a441f63de46bc01dcbdc.png)\n\nConsider the partition of the rectangular region $R$ shown above and the positive function $f(x,y)$ defined on $R.$ Which of the following gives an expression for the lower Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to this partition.\n\n*Hint: ${m}_{ij}$ denotes the minimum value of $f$ on the subregion ${R}_{ij}$*" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the lower Riemann sum $L$ with respect to the given partition, we compute the sum of the volumes of $4$ rectangular solids, one for each ${R}_{ij}.$\n\nThe volume of the rectangular solid corresponding to each subregion ${R}_{ij}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{m}_{ij}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{ij}).\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ denotes the minimum value of $f$ on the subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *minimum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *lower* sum.\n\nSo in our case, we have\n\n$$\nL={m}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{m}_{21}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{21})+{m}_{12}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{12})+{m}_{22}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{22}).\n$$\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}({R}_{11})=\\text{Area}({R}_{21})=\\text{Area}({R}_{12})=\\text{Area}({R}_{22})=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & =1\\cdot {m}_{11}+1\\cdot {m}_{21}+1\\cdot {m}_{12}+1\\cdot {m}_{22} \\\\  & ={m}_{11}+{m}_{21}+{m}_{12}+{m}_{22}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-cee86ad7-df28-501c-a81c-6bd872b01f2a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-cee86ad7-df28-501c-a81c-6bd872b01f2a" :answer-field/id #uuid "cee86ad7-df28-501c-a81c-6bd872b01f2a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-1f4984a1-bf54-50db-b28e-4424d035c287" :answer-field/choices ["answer-12704151-2a3f-5c78-82a6-3698cf12fb79" "answer-1f4984a1-bf54-50db-b28e-4424d035c287" "answer-b62b1dcc-a7a2-515a-82fc-67a62e3f0afa" "answer-81e1aec9-02c9-5d64-aa88-79ce6c1d9935" "answer-ed0995e6-6731-5004-bd04-b2911f5c2cab"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-12704151-2a3f-5c78-82a6-3698cf12fb79" :answer/id #uuid "12704151-2a3f-5c78-82a6-3698cf12fb79" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2({m}_{11}+{m}_{21}+{m}_{12}+{m}_{22})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1f4984a1-bf54-50db-b28e-4424d035c287" :answer/id #uuid "1f4984a1-bf54-50db-b28e-4424d035c287" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{m}_{11}+{m}_{21}+{m}_{12}+{m}_{22}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b62b1dcc-a7a2-515a-82fc-67a62e3f0afa" :answer/id #uuid "b62b1dcc-a7a2-515a-82fc-67a62e3f0afa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{m}_{11}+{m}_{21}-{m}_{12}-{m}_{22}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-81e1aec9-02c9-5d64-aa88-79ce6c1d9935" :answer/id #uuid "81e1aec9-02c9-5d64-aa88-79ce6c1d9935" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{m}_{11}-{m}_{21}-{m}_{12}-{m}_{22}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ed0995e6-6731-5004-bd04-b2911f5c2cab" :answer/id #uuid "ed0995e6-6731-5004-bd04-b2911f5c2cab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{m}_{11}\\cdot {m}_{21}\\cdot {m}_{12}\\cdot {m}_{22}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-cde06bdc-b497-5379-91e5-90582a7fb14e" :question/id #uuid "cde06bdc-b497-5379-91e5-90582a7fb14e" :question/math-academy-id "q-122886" :question/problem "![](images/c9/c9544b511212f20620d516a6f14fcfa1d812a0119cc14f8741d113c6cb663961.png)\n\nConsider the partition of the rectangular region $R$ shown above and the positive function $f(x,y)$ defined on $R.$ Which of the following gives an expression for the lower Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to this partition.\n\n*Hint: ${m}_{ij}$ denotes the minimum value of $f$ on the subregion ${R}_{ij}$*" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the lower Riemann sum $L$ with respect to the given partition, we compute the sum of the volumes of $4$ rectangular solids, one for each ${R}_{ij}.$\n\nThe volume of the rectangular solid corresponding to each subregion ${R}_{ij}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{m}_{ij}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{ij}).\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ denotes the minimum value of $f$ on the subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *minimum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *lower* sum.\n\nSo in our case, we have\n\n$$\nL={m}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{m}_{21}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{21})+{m}_{12}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{12})+{m}_{22}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{22}).\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}({R}_{11})=\\text{Area}({R}_{21})=1,\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}({R}_{12})=\\text{Area}({R}_{22})=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & =1\\cdot {m}_{11}+1\\cdot {m}_{21}+2\\cdot {m}_{12}+2\\cdot {m}_{22} \\\\  & ={m}_{11}+{m}_{21}+2{m}_{12}+2{m}_{22}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-dcb531dc-a984-5ad5-8e3d-3ead33a40597"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-dcb531dc-a984-5ad5-8e3d-3ead33a40597" :answer-field/id #uuid "dcb531dc-a984-5ad5-8e3d-3ead33a40597" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3bdf7f22-f9ed-5577-a8be-e560b2430cc4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9f49662e-9f1d-5dac-a394-6f82ad2e70e6" "answer-dabe35cb-066f-51f0-aee7-336adb36649f" "answer-03d6fd7a-77ba-50da-9b48-5f42b4a3f71c" "answer-3bdf7f22-f9ed-5577-a8be-e560b2430cc4" "answer-0b1831a8-7319-5cf3-9494-86fd997692f2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9f49662e-9f1d-5dac-a394-6f82ad2e70e6" :answer/id #uuid "9f49662e-9f1d-5dac-a394-6f82ad2e70e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2({m}_{11}+{m}_{21}+{m}_{12}+{m}_{22})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dabe35cb-066f-51f0-aee7-336adb36649f" :answer/id #uuid "dabe35cb-066f-51f0-aee7-336adb36649f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{m}_{11}+2{m}_{21}+{m}_{12}+{m}_{22}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-03d6fd7a-77ba-50da-9b48-5f42b4a3f71c" :answer/id #uuid "03d6fd7a-77ba-50da-9b48-5f42b4a3f71c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{m}_{11}+2{m}_{21}+2{m}_{12}+{m}_{22}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3bdf7f22-f9ed-5577-a8be-e560b2430cc4" :answer/id #uuid "3bdf7f22-f9ed-5577-a8be-e560b2430cc4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{m}_{11}+{m}_{21}+2{m}_{12}+2{m}_{22}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0b1831a8-7319-5cf3-9494-86fd997692f2" :answer/id #uuid "0b1831a8-7319-5cf3-9494-86fd997692f2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{m}_{11}+{m}_{21}+{m}_{12}+{m}_{22}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-cfbdcb48-ce24-5aa4-b673-ed006db801e9" :question/id #uuid "cfbdcb48-ce24-5aa4-b673-ed006db801e9" :question/math-academy-id "q-122885" :question/problem "![](images/b0/b00e13fc7b827b9c3960073679ee651f6bce5a6193e0b0af1907738691a287ed.png)\n\nConsider the partition of the rectangular region $R$ shown above and the positive function $f(x,y)$ defined on $R.$ Which of the following gives an expression for the lower Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to this partition.\n\n*Hint: ${m}_{ij}$ denotes the minimum value of $f$ on the subregion ${R}_{ij}$*" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the lower Riemann sum $L$ with respect to the given partition, we compute the sum of the volumes of $3$ rectangular solids, one for each ${R}_{ij}.$\n\nThe volume of the rectangular solid corresponding to each subregion ${R}_{ij}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{m}_{ij}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{ij}).\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ denotes the minimum value of $f$ on the subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *minimum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *lower* sum.\n\nSo in our case, we have\n\n$$\nL={m}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{m}_{21}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{21})+{m}_{12}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{12}).\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}({R}_{11})=1,\n$$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}({R}_{21})=3,\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}({R}_{12})=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & =1\\cdot {m}_{11}+3\\cdot {m}_{21}+2\\cdot {m}_{12} \\\\  & ={m}_{11}+3{m}_{21}+2{m}_{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-366ce63e-4758-55ab-ade5-2bbdeee37bb2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-366ce63e-4758-55ab-ade5-2bbdeee37bb2" :answer-field/id #uuid "366ce63e-4758-55ab-ade5-2bbdeee37bb2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0d188a23-dab3-5b6e-8263-d8a3e3585db8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-bea7801d-9b07-56e2-a485-354d609cc6fd" "answer-c84f6a96-35e9-5f82-ba6e-69dc607bc73c" "answer-8937b8f1-b84c-52e8-97eb-b8be5b9c9cff" "answer-0d188a23-dab3-5b6e-8263-d8a3e3585db8" "answer-d8551ee9-261d-5834-b7b2-72906db68e5d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bea7801d-9b07-56e2-a485-354d609cc6fd" :answer/id #uuid "bea7801d-9b07-56e2-a485-354d609cc6fd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2({m}_{11}+{m}_{21}+{m}_{12})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c84f6a96-35e9-5f82-ba6e-69dc607bc73c" :answer/id #uuid "c84f6a96-35e9-5f82-ba6e-69dc607bc73c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3({m}_{11}+{m}_{21}+{m}_{12})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8937b8f1-b84c-52e8-97eb-b8be5b9c9cff" :answer/id #uuid "8937b8f1-b84c-52e8-97eb-b8be5b9c9cff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{m}_{11}+2{m}_{21}+3{m}_{12}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0d188a23-dab3-5b6e-8263-d8a3e3585db8" :answer/id #uuid "0d188a23-dab3-5b6e-8263-d8a3e3585db8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{m}_{11}+3{m}_{21}+2{m}_{12}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d8551ee9-261d-5834-b7b2-72906db68e5d" :answer/id #uuid "d8551ee9-261d-5834-b7b2-72906db68e5d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{m}_{11}+{m}_{21}+{m}_{12}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152393 :question/problem "![](images/ee/ee1a59d15c7ad98ef2f0dd79d622c74f9fd419fa24db4212fe3bb35030e806a8.png)\n\nConsider the partition of the rectangular region $R$ shown above and the positive function $f(x,y)$ defined on $R.$ Which of the following gives an expression for the lower Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to this partition.\n\n*Hint: ${m}_{ij}$ denotes the minimum value of $f$ on the subregion ${R}_{ij}$*" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the lower Riemann sum $L$ with respect to the given partition, we compute the sum of the volumes of $4$ rectangular solids, one for each ${R}_{ij}.$\n\nThe volume of the rectangular solid corresponding to each subregion ${R}_{ij}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{m}_{ij}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{ij}).\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ denotes the minimum value of $f$ on the subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *minimum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *lower* sum.\n\nSo in our case, we have\n\n$$\nL={m}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{m}_{21}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{21})+{m}_{12}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{12})+{m}_{22}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{22}).\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}({R}_{11})=\\text{Area}({R}_{21})=2\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}({R}_{12})=\\text{Area}({R}_{22})=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & =2\\cdot {m}_{11}+2\\cdot {m}_{21}+{m}_{12}+{m}_{22} \\\\  & =2{m}_{11}+2{m}_{21}+{m}_{12}+{m}_{22}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186148889 :answer-field/correct "answer-9fc5a8e2-26fa-5e37-961f-3fa132a8b42f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-915ebf17-94f8-5c72-ae44-676a73d72d9a" "answer-9fc5a8e2-26fa-5e37-961f-3fa132a8b42f" "answer-2cbb0a6a-df5c-5bc1-8a49-a4c4fdf2a5ff" "answer-35cdbd40-9a06-5e92-a857-4869a4c940eb" "answer-47e58e88-a133-5e35-b49f-24dd21975b15"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-915ebf17-94f8-5c72-ae44-676a73d72d9a" :answer/id #uuid "915ebf17-94f8-5c72-ae44-676a73d72d9a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2({m}_{11}+{m}_{21}+{m}_{12}+{m}_{22})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9fc5a8e2-26fa-5e37-961f-3fa132a8b42f" :answer/id #uuid "9fc5a8e2-26fa-5e37-961f-3fa132a8b42f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{m}_{11}+2{m}_{21}+{m}_{12}+{m}_{22}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2cbb0a6a-df5c-5bc1-8a49-a4c4fdf2a5ff" :answer/id #uuid "2cbb0a6a-df5c-5bc1-8a49-a4c4fdf2a5ff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{m}_{11}+{m}_{21}+{m}_{12}+{m}_{22}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-35cdbd40-9a06-5e92-a857-4869a4c940eb" :answer/id #uuid "35cdbd40-9a06-5e92-a857-4869a4c940eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{m}_{11}-{m}_{21}+{m}_{12}-{m}_{22}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-47e58e88-a133-5e35-b49f-24dd21975b15" :answer/id #uuid "47e58e88-a133-5e35-b49f-24dd21975b15" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{m}_{11}\\cdot {m}_{21}\\cdot {m}_{12}\\cdot {m}_{22}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186256755 :question/problem "Let $R=[0,4]\\times [1,3]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=13-x-{y}^{2}.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{0,1,2,3,4\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{1,3\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the lower Riemann sum $L(f,P).$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-8ad4ccbd-e338-5550-8a1d-a1b82832243e" :question/id #uuid "8ad4ccbd-e338-5550-8a1d-a1b82832243e" :question/math-academy-id "q-122966" :question/problem "Let $R=[1,3]\\times [0,2]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=11-{x}^{2}-y.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{1,2,3\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{0,1,2\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the lower Riemann sum $L(f,P).$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's draw the region $R$ and the partition $P.$\n\n![](images/3b/3be0ba3fa44ba61e0b55500e588387cd087b8d2f2687c5636c9b053f1f8dc5d6.png)\n\nThe lower Riemann sum $L(f,P)$ is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={m}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{m}_{21}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{21})+{m}_{12}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{12})+{m}_{22}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{22})\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ is the minimum value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *minimum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *lower* sum.\n\nTaking into account the fact that $\\text{Area}({R}_{ij})=1$ for all $4$ subregions, the formula for $L(f,P)$ reduces to\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={m}_{11}+{m}_{21}+{m}_{12}+{m}_{22}.\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n- $f(x,y)=11-{x}^{2}-y$ decreases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=11-{x}^{2}-y$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/9f/9fa44875a37e8c7b7bc69b175ac1f30fe73af936565e68ecaa82e02b7617b330.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top right corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](images/59/595d13ca8ec18056038a855e96ca4a3d8cc967182dae5c54b9746c731238413b.png)\n\nHence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{11} & =f(2,1)=6 \\\\ {m}_{21} & =f(3,1)=1 \\\\ {m}_{12} & =f(2,2)=5 \\\\ {m}_{22} & =f(3,2)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\nL(f,P)=6+1+5+0=12.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-14455e9e-ecaa-5111-b90d-483eb946543b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-14455e9e-ecaa-5111-b90d-483eb946543b" :answer-field/id #uuid "14455e9e-ecaa-5111-b90d-483eb946543b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6ade1e9f-48c8-5454-bff2-0de3aabc833c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6ade1e9f-48c8-5454-bff2-0de3aabc833c" "answer-888bac61-eb50-50bf-adde-8d2e2ddef8cf" "answer-688c2410-3624-5fc3-b9cb-d5377915e7cd" "answer-3b3f6271-26ac-5779-9fc0-4fb7ad90aa79" "answer-fa76ed60-6738-528c-9aac-b75fcea7735d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6ade1e9f-48c8-5454-bff2-0de3aabc833c" :answer/id #uuid "6ade1e9f-48c8-5454-bff2-0de3aabc833c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-888bac61-eb50-50bf-adde-8d2e2ddef8cf" :answer/id #uuid "888bac61-eb50-50bf-adde-8d2e2ddef8cf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-688c2410-3624-5fc3-b9cb-d5377915e7cd" :answer/id #uuid "688c2410-3624-5fc3-b9cb-d5377915e7cd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3b3f6271-26ac-5779-9fc0-4fb7ad90aa79" :answer/id #uuid "3b3f6271-26ac-5779-9fc0-4fb7ad90aa79" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fa76ed60-6738-528c-9aac-b75fcea7735d" :answer/id #uuid "fa76ed60-6738-528c-9aac-b75fcea7735d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186256758 :question/problem "Let $R=[1,3]\\times [1,3]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=13-2x-2y.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{1,2,3\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{1,2,3\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the lower Riemann sum $L(f,P).$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-68f740c4-3eaf-53af-86af-a7b05d82500b" :question/id #uuid "68f740c4-3eaf-53af-86af-a7b05d82500b" :question/math-academy-id "q-75253" :question/problem "Let $R=[0,4]\\times [0,4]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=20-2x-3y.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{0,2,4\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{0,2,4\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the lower Riemann sum $L(f,P).$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's draw the region $R$ and the partition $P.$\n\n![](images/29/293e79685a3f4da205d986bcf4331e4b4f43c0a48fe183d27f93aaee6bb17b99.png)\n\nThe lower Riemann sum $L(f,P)$ is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={m}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{m}_{21}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{21})+{m}_{12}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{12})+{m}_{22}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{22})\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ is the minimum value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *minimum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *lower* sum.\n\nTaking into account the fact that $\\text{Area}({R}_{ij})=4$ for all $4$ subregions, the formula for $L(f,P)$ reduces to\n\n$$\nL(f,P)=4{m}_{11}+4{m}_{21}+4{m}_{12}+4{m}_{22}.\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n- $f(x,y)=20-2x-3y$ decreases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=20-2x-3y$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/cc/cc6e04660f00d04307715159c25aa2860ca08af74ed36fc9b0be15d10ee94a27.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top right corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](images/74/744aeb24bb4fd4487b35ffd789d957879cb0c3ee92e40519f71b65ee5ee76dcf.png)\n\nHence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{11} & =f(2,2)=10 \\\\ {m}_{21} & =f(4,2)=6 \\\\ {m}_{12} & =f(2,4)=4 \\\\ {m}_{22} & =f(4,4)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\nL(f,P)=4\\cdot 10+4\\cdot 6+4\\cdot 4+4\\cdot 0=80.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-85c51992-c8f6-553a-ab49-de91cc2fad16"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-85c51992-c8f6-553a-ab49-de91cc2fad16" :answer-field/id #uuid "85c51992-c8f6-553a-ab49-de91cc2fad16" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0cd184c5-a1ab-5ea2-a565-dc9e11d0577f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a9a25326-be2d-5c80-8dde-5f079287a42f" "answer-b81ae7bf-dac2-515c-8794-1cd63313830e" "answer-1d9bb78a-6144-5f51-9960-0c3b78126ad5" "answer-47051153-0c3e-51ec-b6c0-503c70ae170b" "answer-0cd184c5-a1ab-5ea2-a565-dc9e11d0577f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a9a25326-be2d-5c80-8dde-5f079287a42f" :answer/id #uuid "a9a25326-be2d-5c80-8dde-5f079287a42f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "100" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b81ae7bf-dac2-515c-8794-1cd63313830e" :answer/id #uuid "b81ae7bf-dac2-515c-8794-1cd63313830e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "120" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1d9bb78a-6144-5f51-9960-0c3b78126ad5" :answer/id #uuid "1d9bb78a-6144-5f51-9960-0c3b78126ad5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "40" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-47051153-0c3e-51ec-b6c0-503c70ae170b" :answer/id #uuid "47051153-0c3e-51ec-b6c0-503c70ae170b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "60" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0cd184c5-a1ab-5ea2-a565-dc9e11d0577f" :answer/id #uuid "0cd184c5-a1ab-5ea2-a565-dc9e11d0577f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "80" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152396 :question/problem "Let $R=[0,3]\\times [0,2]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=6-x-y.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{0,1,2,3\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{0,2\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the lower Riemann sum $L(f,P).$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's draw the region $R$ and the partition $P.$\n\n![](images/17/178108b256e55eaa5bd58c72f606fbed0aef774ff10a46e059c70abe93f8b341.png)\n\nThe lower Riemann sum $L(f,P)$ is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={m}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{m}_{21}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{21})+{m}_{31}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{31})\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ is the minimum value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *minimum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *lower* sum.\n\nTaking into account the fact that $\\text{Area}({R}_{ij})=2$ for all $3$ subregions, the formula for $L(f,P)$ reduces to\n\n$$\nL(f,P)=2{m}_{11}+2{m}_{21}+2{m}_{31}.\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n- $f(x,y)=6-x-y$ decreases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=6-x-y$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/dd/dd521e876abfc4313afb5beaf568c1d93cad670cfa912e210ed5d1548c51ec97.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top right corner* of each subregion. \n\n![](images/05/0515af2764a6ac27b2b69998ea4b99079dd7266a5989a161d01a6d25a670678e.png)\n\nHence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{11} & =f(1,2)=3 \\\\ {m}_{21} & =f(2,2)=2 \\\\ {m}_{31} & =f(3,2)=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\nL(f,P)=2\\cdot 3+2\\cdot 2+2\\cdot 1=12.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186148907 :answer-field/correct 17592186148908 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186345023 :question/problem "Let $R=[0,2]\\times [0,2]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=x+y+10.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{0,1,2\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{0,1,2\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the lower Riemann sum $L(f,P).$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186345051 :question/problem "Let $R=[1,3]\\times [1,4]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=x+y.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{1,2,3\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{1,2,3,4\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the lower Riemann sum $L(f,P).$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152710 :question/problem "Let $R=[1,3]\\times [1,3]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=x+y+1.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{1,2,3\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{1,2,3\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the lower Riemann sum $L(f,P).$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186256763 :question/problem "Let $R=[1,4]\\times [0,2]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=x+{y}^{2}+2.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{1,2,3,4\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{0,2\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the lower Riemann sum $L(f,P).$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-73bd1c38-9ed6-5451-94fd-2aa984462a1e" :question/id #uuid "73bd1c38-9ed6-5451-94fd-2aa984462a1e" :question/math-academy-id "q-75039" :question/problem "Let $R=[2,4]\\times [2,4]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{2,3,4\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{2,3,4\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the lower Riemann sum $L(f,P).$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's draw the region $R$ and the partition $P.$\n\n![](images/a3/a30d43569026cdf8f4ce960016620a725248726523abd005dbad5bc903123b9f.png)\n\nThe lower sum $L(f,P)$ is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={m}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{m}_{21}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{21})+{m}_{12}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{12})+{m}_{22}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{22})\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *minimum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *lower* sum.\n\nTaking into account the fact that $\\text{Area}({R}_{ij})=1$ for all $4$ subregions, the formula for $L(f,P)$ reduces to\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={m}_{11}+{m}_{21}+{m}_{12}+{m}_{22}.\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n- $f(x,y)={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/a8/a81396ee6d33b1ac10a44b6b8db2ded2612e86274e017ebe95c55420b7f73265.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom left corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](images/c9/c90a6e6d4c9e9a92bfd1c42b8350941b7d45f96d422e2a1988a4c003df6457e1.png)\n\nHence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{11} & =f(2,2)=8 \\\\ {m}_{21} & =f(3,2)=13 \\\\ {m}_{12} & =f(2,3)=13 \\\\ {m}_{22} & =f(3,3)=18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & =8+13+13+18 \\\\  & =52.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-08a4ee6d-5997-53cb-a03a-d8841c187de9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-08a4ee6d-5997-53cb-a03a-d8841c187de9" :answer-field/id #uuid "08a4ee6d-5997-53cb-a03a-d8841c187de9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ac8d42e0-eaa9-505b-8931-064524f4bd68" :answer-field/choices ["answer-88b3a027-2fb3-5589-8df2-d6ac588524bc" "answer-f58f6e34-2e0f-5f5d-832d-5b3725016996" "answer-107dfb62-1b9d-51c8-9744-e1f29dd07655" "answer-ac8d42e0-eaa9-505b-8931-064524f4bd68" "answer-ba6dcd45-400c-5812-8da7-5f3fb8564611"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-88b3a027-2fb3-5589-8df2-d6ac588524bc" :answer/id #uuid "88b3a027-2fb3-5589-8df2-d6ac588524bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "34" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f58f6e34-2e0f-5f5d-832d-5b3725016996" :answer/id #uuid "f58f6e34-2e0f-5f5d-832d-5b3725016996" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "42" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-107dfb62-1b9d-51c8-9744-e1f29dd07655" :answer/id #uuid "107dfb62-1b9d-51c8-9744-e1f29dd07655" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "48" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ac8d42e0-eaa9-505b-8931-064524f4bd68" :answer/id #uuid "ac8d42e0-eaa9-505b-8931-064524f4bd68" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "52" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ba6dcd45-400c-5812-8da7-5f3fb8564611" :answer/id #uuid "ba6dcd45-400c-5812-8da7-5f3fb8564611" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "57" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186153349 :tutorial/content "In this lesson, we will describe a process for calculating a **lower bound** for the volume enclosed between a surface $z=f(x,y)$ and the $xy$-plane. \n\nAs an example, consider the rectangle $R$ in the $xy$-plane, defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nA sketch of the region $R$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/bf/bf7ef4752b0910b5544707eef97c854d8eeeedbc221a81c5fa631cf38b8b8d9a.png)\n\nNow consider the function $f(x,y) = 3-x^2-y^2,$ defined over $R,$ shown below.\n\n![](images/34/34f7936b29e6a177ae0c831e36654dc5059514580a1947324a40d52320b83e5a.png)\n\n \n\nThe space underneath the surface and above the region $R$ defines a fixed volume $V.$ Our goal is to find a lower bound for $V.$ We do this by approximating this volume using rectangular solids. \n\nWe start by partitioning the $x$- and $y$-intervals of $R.$ Let's pick two subintervals of equal length for both $x$ and $y.$\n\n![](images/c3/c375b605ca6b7d7f2935218976f5e09db5ed2cfb64d811b1fe0a854d02646a36.png)\n\nThe region $R$ is now partitioned into $4$ rectangles:\n\n![](images/20/2026210e2cd58b2f2f7290a2d4f4186875903d146d02597787393727afd7f6a6.png)\n\nWe seek a *lower* bound for the volume $V.$ So, we let $m_{ij}$ be the *smallest* value of $f$ in each subregion $R_{ij}.$ We then define a rectangular solid in each subregion whose base is $R_{ij}$ and whose height is $m_{ij}.$ \n\nFor example, the rectangular solid corresponding to $R_{11}$ is given below. \n\n![](images/43/4324b984fb1056750f9bfceda58d57b2e0dbf1875ff21479d5ef93f088bfc50b.png)\n\n \n\nThe volume of this rectangular solid is\n\n$$\nm_{11}\\cdot \\textrm{Area}(R_{11})  = \\dfrac14m_{11}.\n$$\n\nSimilarly, the volumes of the rectangular solids formed by the partitions $R_{21}, R_{12},$ and $R_{22}$ respectively are\n\n$$\n\\dfrac14m_{21}, \\qquad \\dfrac14m_{12}, \\qquad \\dfrac14m_{22}.\n$$\n\nDrawing all four rectangular solids, we get a volume that looks as follows:\n\n![](images/89/89d3706148d3f52096f94287c9cf4694b281bab18a8803bafe1b67d81e9b87fc.png)\n\n \n\nThe lower bound $L$ for our volume is the sum of the volumes of our four rectangular solids. This gives\n\n$$\nL = \\dfrac14(m_{11} + m_{21}+ m_{12}+m_{22}).\n$$\n\nThe number $L$ is called the **lower Riemann sum with respect to the given partition**.\n\n**Note:** We don't yet know the values of $m_{ij},$ the height of each solid. We'll learn to figure these out a little later in the lesson. For now, we will just focus on writing $L$ as an expression of $m_{ij}.$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152325 :activity/expected-seconds 660.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
